    "result_text": "Both tests pass and the full build is green. Here's a summary of what I changed.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe identity key is now a single SHA-256 value, and duplicate detection (409) keys off it.\n\n**New identity key** (`OwnerIdentity.java`) \u2014 now the lowercase hex SHA-256 of `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)`. Previously it was an un-hashed `telephone|email|householdId` string. The `householdId` segment is gone, so `householdId` is no longer part of identity (it's still computed and used for household size / membership-level capping).\n\n**Soundex** (`OwnerSoundex.java`, new) \u2014 standard American Soundex, shared by both the identity key and the soft-match rule so phonetically-alike surnames collapse to the same code in both places.\n\n**Hard duplicate \u2192 409** (new):\n- `CheckOwnerDuplicateIdentity` \u2014 scans existing owners for a matching identity key, skipping soft-deleted ones, and throws the checked `OwnerDuplicateIdentityException`.\n- `OwnerDuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler` + escalation YAML map that to **409 Conflict**.\n- Wired into `owners.POST.yml` as a `checkDuplicateIdentity` step between `build` and `assignHousehold` (after `validate`, so the email-domain blocklist is still applied first).\n\n**Soft match redesigned** (`FlagOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java`) \u2014 now flags when the identity key *differs* but `soundex(lastName)` and postcode both match (still ignoring deleted owners and still exempting declared `sharesHousehold` members). Previously it matched on exact last name + postcode + *different* telephone.\n\n## Behaviour change this produces\nTwo owners with the same last name and postcode but **different telephones** now get different identity keys, so they're no longer a hard 409 \u2014 they're created as a soft match. The old household-id-based 409 path is gone entirely (it isn't reintroduced anywhere).\n\nTest results: `AcceptanceTest` (`coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex`, `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity`) \u2014 2 run, 0 failures; full suite **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
